import InteractingSLE.Spec.Sec5.Lemma47AnglePass

/-!
# Lemma 4.7's chart clause on the glued space for an arbitrary good set

Packet PROVE-CFCHART. The glued-space chart clause of the counterflow's killed image word
(`Lemma47Angle.isChartCouplingCharFunConst_q_angle`) is stated for the good set `glueGood47 μ`, the complement of a
measurable hull of the bad samples **in the full product σ-algebra**. The transfer to the given space (PROVE-CFGIVEN
§3, step 4) needs a good set that is measurable for a coarser σ-algebra (generated by the field, the flow data and the
counterflow history), on which the glued measure and the law of the given space agree. The four results below are the
proofs of `Lemma47AngleIdent` / `Lemma47AnglePass` with the good set `E` a parameter: they only use that every sample
of `E` is good (`hEg`), that `E` is measurable and that almost every glued sample lies in `E`.

## Main results

* `ae_condExp_glue_eq_neg_chartMean_E`, `ae_condExp_glue_eq_qF_E` (step R1 at a counterflow time);
* `ae_condExp_qRaw_eq_qF_E` (the passage to fixed image times of the raw image filtration);
* **`isChartCouplingCharFunConst_q_E`**: the chart coupling clause of `−h` at fixed image times of `qRaw … E`.

R48: nothing here uses Theorem 1.2/1.3, `Theorem12ParamStatement`, `Theorem13Statement` or any `*_of_param`.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

noncomputable section

